---
title: "Zazz 0.8 alpha"
description: "Zazz 0.8 alpha puts radius on the spacing scale, adds a numeric --elevation drawn as a layered box-shadow, and adds filter and blend utilities."
date: 2026-10-19
draft: false
tags: ["release"]
---

**Zazz 0.8 alpha puts radius on the spacing scale, adds an `--elevation` utility whose shadow is computed from a single number, and adds filter and blend utilities. It also renames `--rounded`, `--shadow-hue`, and every primitive's `-rounded` hook, and changes the dialog sizes, so this is a breaking release.**

## `--radius` takes a number

`--rounded` was Tailwind's name for a raw `border-radius`. 0.8 renames it [`--radius`](/api/utilities/borders/) and puts it on the same scale as spacing. A number is that many `--spacing` steps times `--radius-multiplier`, so `--radius: 2.5` is exactly `--radius-md`:

```html
<div style="--radius: 2.5"></div>           <!-- --radius-md -->
<div style="--radius: 1rem"></div>          <!-- a length passes through -->
<div style="--radius: full"></div>          <!-- a pill -->
<div style="--radius: 1; --radius--hover: 4; --radius--md: 2.5"></div>
```

It takes states and breakpoints, and `--radius-multiplier` still squares or softens the whole kit at once. A value with several corners doesn't fit a single number, so four side utilities round two corners each: `--radius-t: 2.5` rounds a card's media along the top. The primitives' hooks follow the rename (`--ui-button-radius`), and each primitive's main radius hook takes a number too. A hook takes one value now, so a hook with several corners renders square.

## `--elevation`

I wanted a shadow you set by height, the way you set padding by a number. [`--elevation`](/api/utilities/effects/) draws four box-shadow layers from one value:

```html
<div style="--elevation: 1.5; --elevation--hover: 4"></div>
```

Each layer sits farther out along the light than the one before it and blurs in proportion. As the number rises, the blurred far layers fade in and darken, so a low element has a tight contact shadow and a high one gets a soft, wide spread. The layer offsets and blur ratios come from the old `--shadow-2xl`, which was already a stack of scaled layers, and the opacities were tuned by eye in a prototype. `--elevation: 4` uses the same layers as `--shadow-md`.

Each layer also pulls in by a negative spread, and blurs by no more than its distance, so with the light overhead a shadow never shows above the element or past its sides: a card sits on its shadow instead of being outlined by it. It shares one `box-shadow` with `--ring` and `--shadow`: a ring or a primitive's focus ring draws first and keeps the elevation, and an explicit `--shadow` replaces it.

## Shadow tokens and light

The `--shadow-2xs` … `2xl` tokens are now drawn with the same formula, so `--shadow: var(--shadow-md)` and `--elevation: 4` look alike. `--shadow` is the box-shadow form: a token or any box-shadow. The size words (`--shadow: md`) are gone; write `var(--shadow-md)`.

Two theme inputs set the light for the page: `--color-shadow` for the color and the new `--default-shadow-angle` for the direction. `--shadow-tint` (renamed from `--shadow-hue`) and `--shadow-angle` change them for an element and its subtree, so a bottom sheet can cast its shadow up.

## Filters and blending

[`--filter`, `--backdrop-filter`, and `--mix-blend`](/api/utilities/effects/) set `filter`, `backdrop-filter`, and `mix-blend-mode`. They take state tiers and have pseudo-element forms, and a tier works on its own: `--filter: grayscale(1); --filter--hover: none` colors a logo when you hover it, and `--filter--hover: blur(2px)` by itself leaves the element sharp at rest.

The lightbox used to darken a hovered stage image with its own `filter`, which would have fought the utility. It no longer sets `filter` at all; the migration list below has the two lines that bring the dimming back.

## Dialog sizes follow the layout

[`data-dialog-size`](/api/primitives/dialog/) takes the layout's sizes now: `sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xl`, and `2xl` cap a dialog at that band's width, `full` spans the screen inside the gutters, and `bleed` fills it edge to edge. With no size a dialog is `sm`, 40rem, which is a little wider than the old 50ch default.

```html
<dialog data-ui="dialog" data-dialog-size="lg">…</dialog>
```

## Smaller things

`--top`, `--right`, `--bottom`, and `--left` take `auto`, so a side you set at one breakpoint can go back to `auto` at another. A bar can stick to the bottom on a phone and to the top on a desktop: `--bottom: 0; --bottom--lg: auto; --top: auto; --top--lg: 0`.

Reveals run a bit slower and travel farther by default (1000ms and 2rem), and `--ui-reveal-global-stagger-step` sets the delay between a group's children for everything below it.

## Migrating

- `--rounded` → `--radius`, and `--ui-<primitive>-rounded` → `--ui-<primitive>-radius`. A token value still works (`--radius: var(--radius-md)`), or write its number (`2.5`).
- A multi-corner `--rounded` value or hook → the side utilities (`--radius-t: 2.5`), or a single value.
- `--shadow: md` → `--shadow: var(--shadow-md)`, or `--elevation: 4`.
- `--shadow-hue` → `--shadow-tint`.
- `data-dialog-size="article"` → `"sm"` (or no size), `"container"` → `"md"`, and `"screen"` → `"bleed"`. The mobile menu uses `"bleed"` now.
- The lightbox no longer darkens a hovered image. To keep it, put `data-ui="group"` on the slide and `--group-filter--hover: brightness(0.8)` on the image.

The [changelog](https://github.com/dereknelsen/zazz-ui/blob/main/packages/core/CHANGELOG.md) lists every change, including the hook renames for each primitive.
